# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  SecretBeans starter rules - checking and savings exports
#
#  Written by Claude (Anthropic) with Edwin West, August 2026.
#  Not an Anthropic product. See PROVENANCE.md.
#
#  This template has only been tried against Chase exports. Check 'fields'
#  against your own CSV's column order before trusting anything it produces.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Starter rules for a checking or savings export.
#
# Adjust 'fields' to your CSV's own column order, then add 'if' blocks below.
# Column names in 'fields' are hledger's, not the bank's: the ones that matter are
# date, description and amount. Name a column you do not need anything at all, or
# leave the slot empty.

skip 1
# 'bankbalance' rather than 'balance' on purpose. hledger treats a field named
# 'balance' as a BALANCE ASSERTION, which then fails on any transaction you
# deliberately skip - such as the far side of an internal transfer. Naming it
# something hledger does not recognise keeps the column and drops the assertion.
fields  details, date, description, amount, type, bankbalance, checknumber
date-format %-m/%-d/%Y
currency $

account1 assets:bank:CHANGEME

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Categories. Later blocks win, so put general rules first and specific
# exceptions after them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------

# if %description NATIONAL GRID
#   account2 expenses:house:utilities:gas

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Anything with no rule lands in expenses:unknown, which the build reports.
# Resist the urge to add a catch-all - it hides problems rather than fixing them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------

# Checks cannot be identified from a description - 'CHECK 114' says nothing.
# Send them somewhere visible instead of guessing.
if %type CHECK_PAID
  account2 expenses:review:check

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Internal transfers - see docs/TRANSFERS.md. Keep these at the END of the file.
#
# A transfer between two accounts you own appears on BOTH statements. Exactly one
# side must record it or it is counted twice, with every expense figure still
# looking perfectly correct.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------

# if %description Transfer (from|to) SAV.*3456
#   account2 assets:bank:savings

# A card payment is recorded from the CARD statement, which knows which card was
# paid. Skipping it here prevents a duplicate.
# if %description CREDIT CRD
#   skip
